After what seems like a lifetime of playing Nethack 3.1.3 (makes it sound like
a chore) I managed to ascend (some spoilers to follow). I was still hurting
after losing a barbarian that had found my first ever wand of wishing to an
electric eel on the medusa level a few days earlier.

Helga the Valkyrie started with 18 strength, dex and constitution. After a
few levels I found a helm of telepathy in a shop. A stethoscope had been
carelessly left laying around. Then just a little later
a polished silver shield. Things were looking up. At this point I decided that
the castle was the key to a successful game. I entered the gnomish mines, and
had a wonderful time in the mine town. One of the shops had a pair of speed
boots, and the lighting shop had a magic lamp. I also picked up a nice little
deal on a tinning kit. I used the lamp to wish for a
blessed rustproof +1 gray dragon scale mail. I was a little hesitant to wear
my speed boots at first, until I could rustproof them, but after a while I
didn't worry. After grabbing the luckstone at the bottom of the mines, I
felt ready to tackle the castle, having reflection, RoC and low AC, even though
I was only at experience level 12. So down, down, down I went. At the medusa
level I genocided eels, and then realised I couldn't get across the water.
But when I went up a level, a trapdoor dropped me down two levels, so I
decided to attack the castle. I nuked the drawbridge with a wand of striking.
After firing many arrows at the creatures in the doorway, I realised I couldn't
cross the moat. But searching through my bag I found a potion of levitation
that did the trick. I headed straight for the 4 corner rooms until I found
the wand of wishing. I already had a blessed scroll of charging, so I wished
for:
blessed rustproof +1 Mjollnir
blessed rustproof +1 Gauntlets of Power
3 blessed potions of gain ability
blessed bag of holding
blessed ring of levitation
2 blessed amulets of life saving
2 blessed wands of polymorph

I also found a Hawaiian Shirt in another castle room. Suddenly Helga was
looking good! I went back up to the Quest, pausing only to give Medusa
some of her own medicine via my shield of reflection, and on the first quest
level to convert lots of potions to holy water. On the way I procured a
unicorn horn. Solving the Quest was very easy, with Mjollnir doing all of
the talking. I gained the orb of fate and the chime of opening.
Descending again I found Fort Knox, and after beating the crap out of a
zillion soldiers took my gold tally to around $50000. I went straight to a
temple, and some generous donations removed about 9 points from my AC. A few
other blessed scrolls of enchant armour had taken me down to -27 AC, where
it stayed for the rest of the game. A few wands of create monster and some
pious devotion on another altar an I was granted Vorpal Blade (you'd never
know that I hang out on alt.atheism, would you?) I saw two other artifacts
later on, Grimtooth and Giantslayer, but didn't even bother to pick them up.
I went down to the valley of the dead, but only one wraith left a corpse,
taking me to around level 19. Having a ring to teleport control, I thought
I'd level teleport down to the bottom, but I wasn't sure where that was. I
asked for 60, and got "Sorry", ending up on 51. Trudging up level by level,
I went through a portal and killed the Wiz of Yen, to get the book of the
dead. After he'd been born again a few times and Mjollnir and I had escorted
him back to the grave, I realised I'd done things in the wrong order. I
still didn't even know where the stairs to Vlad's tower were. I used the
paralyse by the stairs "bug" to freeze the Wiz for a while (he gets old real
fast!) and started hunting for Vlad. This took me a long time. I tried reading
all the spellbooks in my bag of holding, and found some useful ones: identify,
magic mapping, remove curse. At exp. level 30 it's easy reading. When I finally
found Vlad, he only lasted 3 hits! They don't make super vampires like they
used to. Scurrying down with the candelabrum, I found I couldn't level teleport
to 52, so settled for 51. It took a while to find the vibrating square, but
when I finally got there I'm sure Helga was happy. Performing the arcane ritual
opened the path to Moloch's lair. No real opposition down there at all,
although
I did get scales over my eyes from attacking the priestess. Grabbed the amulet,
and up I went. Past the wiz, and I didn't have any more potions of paralysis.
Level teleported down several times when going up stairs, due to the amulet.
Wearing the ring of levitation seemed to help somewhat. The wiz was pissed.
Powered onto the first endgame level before I realised that I needed more
stuff to locate the portals with. One gold detection scroll got me out of
earth.
I polypiled scrolls on air, giving me a charging scroll that I used on the Orb
of fate to find the way out. But on the way there, ARRRRGHHHHHH!!!!!!!!!!!
I threw Mjollnir and a monster, and it didn't come back! Searching for it later
it just seemed to have vanished. Moving was now very tricky. When the wiz
attacked it was downright nasty. That guy is more persistent than a
Scientologist on a street corner. Eventually I cockatriced him. I resorted to
throwing gems, and got to fire. The Orb of Fate was sulking, and Vorpal Blade
just doesn't cut it :-) next to Mjollnir. But I just went along row by row,
until I was whisked away to water. The Orb agreed to talk nicely now, and
soon I was at the astral plane. A friendly angel greeted me. Everybody else
was somewhat more hostile. Death stopped by for an early grave. After a little
while I got bored, and made a headlong dash for the central altar. I dipped the
amulet in holy water just in case, and offered it skywards.

The highlights:
8.4 million points,
4100 monsters killed,
Killed the Wizard of Yendor 43 times.

About four days of fun! What a game!
